./xmodel/sol-avenues2.md:226:Abandon this as a new constraint source if, in every viable positive-genus passport sector, all adjoint pairings lie in the radical of the existing J plus no-log ideal and give no rank/codimension gain at two generic primes followed by an exact leading-symbol check. Also abandon it until more tail data exists if unresolved B/x coefficients enter before every usable residue order. A genus-zero sector merely gives no conditions in that sector; it does not by itself refute the positive-genus computation.
./xmodel/sol-avenues2.md:290:## 7. Multibranch Gorenstein value-semigroup symmetry at y-infinity
./xmodel/sol-avenues2.md:297:2. Its multivalue semigroup and conductor vector obey Gorenstein/Delgado symmetry constraints.
./xmodel/sol-avenues2.md:298:3. Compute the semigroup from the orbit-compressed parametrizations of \(x,y,h_1,h_2\) and their standard-basis cancellations.
./xmodel/sol-avenues2.md:299:4. Those cancellations see coefficients and can change when the forced levels 38–42 turn on, even though the splice graph passes.
