./phase0-mo-answer-draft.md:17:The baseline is the Newton-polygon program of Guccione, Guccione and Valqui, raised with Horruitiner in [arXiv:2204.14178](https://arxiv.org/abs/2204.14178) to $\max(\deg P,\deg Q)\ge 108$: below degree $125$ a single family survives, $(72,108)$ up to order, reduced by their Prop. 4.3 to two explicit supports with $[P,Q]=x^2$. Everything at $(72,108)$ is conditional on that reduction, whose supporting chain is partly arXiv-only. The elimination of both supports, hence the bound $125$ stated in ratto3423's answer, now has a public, replicated record: Helali ([10.5281/zenodo.21479814](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21479814), first, July 21), Suzuki ([21483636](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21483636)), Ishihara ([21757679](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21757679)); these three are the public replicated record for that elimination, and I have replayed the Helali and Suzuki artifacts exactly. Strinz ([21633408](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21633408)) runs a parallel audited program whose own abstract marks its case closure open, and Leox reports a further independent elimination in the comments here, which I have not checked.
./RECON.md:7:1. **We are not alone on (72,108) — but nobody has landed it properly.** Two public exclusion claims: Helali (07-21, Zenodo 21479814 + GitHub: 89 MB char-0 unit-ideal certificates, conditional on GGHV Prop 4.3, AI-built, unaudited, no arXiv) and Suzuki (07-22, Zenodo 21483636: dessins/Bézout/weighted-Macaulay exclusion of the (8,28) case, 5 MB verification pack), plus an artifact-less echo (Qiu, 08-01). No peer review, no expert endorsement, no GGV contact; openconjectures.org still shows the pre-125 status. A rigorously audited certificate (our lane) can still be the authoritative settlement — and their transcriptions are cross-check material for our Generator A audit.
./RECON.md:9:3. **New structural results we can use:** Shaska 2607.20210v2 (07-25) — in dim 2, graded-equivariant Keller maps are automorphisms for *every* weight sign pattern; Wilson 2607.23887 (07-26) — two-variable Gaussian Moments Conjecture *proved* by Newton-polygon **face isolation**; Speyer-thread Picard obstruction ("only d=3 threads the needle"); Suzuki's 5-class dessin classification of the (8,28) top edge.
