   478	tower of `sol-k2c.md`.
   479	
   480	1. Its reduced type is `(1,2)`, not `(2,3)`. The coordinate-cusp exclusion
   481	   requires both weights greater than one. For `(1,2)`,
   482	   \[
   483	      h(U,V)=V-U^2
   484	   \]
   485	   is a coordinate and
   486	   \[
   487	      h(Z,Z^2)=0.                                                        \tag{6.1}
   488	   \]
   489	   Thus the exact step forbidden by Theorem 2.2 is available.
   490	2. Each displayed recurrence stage is the polynomial automorphism `H_q`.
   491	   Lemma 2.1 applies, so the displayed high-degree representative is not
   492	   degree-minimal. Applying the inverse tower gives the identity pair, with
   493	   degree pair `(1,1)` and pole denominator `1`.
   494	3. Before minimization, the generic coordinate fiber has degree
   495	   `kappa_r`, genus zero, and one singularity at infinity with
   496	   \[
   497	      \delta_\infty
   498	      =\frac{(\kappa_r-1)(\kappa_r-2)}2.                                \tag{6.2}
   499	   \]
   500	   Hence even a large positive embedded conductor is not an Aut-orbit
   501	   invariant. After minimization the fiber is a line and this conductor is
   502	   zero.
   503	
   504	Thus no assertion here would bound the nonminimal Hénon presentation. The
   505	only conditional bound, Theorem 5.1, uses degree minimality exactly where the
   506	Hénon family fails it. Conversely, Theorem 2.2 explains why the same escape
   507	is unavailable merely from a type-`(2,3)` cusp leading form.
   508	
   509	## 7. Final disposition
   510	
   511	\[
   512	\begin{array}{c|c}
   513	\text{attack}&\text{verdict}\\ \hline
   514	\text{degree minimality / approximate roots}
   515	 &\text{removable tails die, but the }(2,3)\text{ cusp protects every scale}\\
   516	J=\text{const}+\text{passport}+\text{handshake}
   517	 &\operatorname{ord}_t f_y=3-\kappa_i;\ 
   518	   Z\text{-order}=5B-2\text{ grows with }B\\
   519	\text{semigroup / conductor}
   520	 &c(P_i)\geq2(\kappa_i-1)\text{ is a lower bound; no fixed upper budget}
   521	\end{array}                                                             \tag{7.1}
   522	\]
   523	
   524	There is no unconditional `K_A`. Under the explicit global-coordinate-tail
   525	hypothesis, `K_A=42`; under the explicit scale bound \(B\leq B_A\),
   526	`K_A=2B_A`.
   527	
   528	The evidence does **not** presently support UCD-A-min as a consequence of
   529	degree minimality, constant Jacobian, the tetrahedral passport, or ordinary
   530	semigroup theory. The exact cusp theorem removes the main proposed source of
   531	support: in reduced type `(2,3)`, degree minimality is automatic at arbitrary
   532	common scale. Nonautomorphy forces the hypothetical pair into the nonproper
   533	Keller sector, but no available nonproperness theorem turns that qualitative
   534	fact into a scale or conductor ceiling. The conjecture may still be true
   535	because the lower Puiseux
   536	coefficient equations might forbid every large-scale polynomial Keller
   537	realization, but that is precisely the unproved algebraization/exclusion
   538	wall.
   539	
   540	\[
   541	 \boxed{\textbf{UCD-A-min is itself the G2 crux; a counterexample sequence,
   542	 if one exists, can live in the non-removable type-}(2,3)\textbf{ carrier
   543	 direction.}}                                                          \tag{7.2}
   544	\]

